-# Living Survey: Quantum_Computing                                                                                  
-                                                                                                                    
-## Introduction                                                                                                     
-                                                                                                                    
-This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Quantum_Computing**.                                   
-                                                                                                                    
-## Foundational Concepts and Architectures                                                                          
-                                                                                                                    
-Recent research continues to explore novel computational paradigms beyond traditional transistor and qubit systems. 
Atom computing has been proposed as an alternative where atoms replace transistors, utilizing controlled flows of    
single electrons or photons for deterministic switching, potentially overcoming material scaling                     
constraints[^10.34257_gjsfra257362]. Furthermore, comparative analyses of future computing architectures highlight   
the distinct potential of quantum systems alongside digital and biological computers, emphasizing the need for       
standardized engineering descriptions and industry models[^10.1109_mc.2021.3083430].                                 
-                                                                                                                    
-## Quantum Algorithms and Optimization                                                                              
-                                                                                                                    
-The application of quantum algorithms to optimization problems remains a vibrant area of study. Hybrid and granular 
approaches have been introduced to enhance quantum genetic optimization, allowing digital computers to evaluate      
fitness functions while quantum processors evolve genetic populations, effectively reducing search space complexity  
even on limited-qubit devices[^10.1007_s41066-022-00348-9]. Additionally, empirical investigations into developer    
ecosystems reveal that hybrid quantum-classical computing and quantum circuit implementation are the most prevalent  
topics in practitioner discussions, with Qiskit and Q-sharp dominating the toolchain landscape alongside frequent    
references to Grover's and Shor's algorithms[^https:__openalex.org_W7155247427].                                     
-                                                                                                                    
-## Quantum Simulation and Materials Science                                                                         
-                                                                                                                    
-Quantum computing is increasingly applied to computational chemistry and materials science. Practical guides        
demonstrate how quantum annealers can calculate the relative energy of defective structures, such as graphene, by    
translating chemical models into qubit representations[^10.1063_5.0151346]. In the realm of fluid dynamics, quantum  
algorithms based on the Lattice Boltzmann Method have been developed to simulate 2D flows around cylinders,          
demonstrating the applicability of quantum computing to industrial CFD problems despite early-stage implementation   
challenges[^10.21741_9781644902813-38][^10.11159_icffts23.133]. Software tools like PULSEE also bridge quantum       
information science and magnetic resonance, simulating spin time evolution and quantum gates to investigate emergent 
quantum order in strongly correlated materials[^10.1016_j.cpc.2022.108598].                                          
-                                                                                                                    
-## Quantum Cryptography and Security                                                                                
-                                                                                                                    
-The intersection of quantum mechanics and cryptography continues to evolve. Educational and simulation works detail 
the implementation of the BB84 quantum key distribution (QKD) protocol, modeling quantum state preparation,          
eavesdropping attacks, and classical post-processing to demonstrate provably secure                                  
communication[^10.6084_m9.figshare.32051724]. Academic theses further explore quantum cryptography protocols (BB84,  
B92, B91) and Shor's algorithm, analyzing vulnerabilities such as photon splitting and faked-state attacks in quantum
cryptographic systems[^https:__openalex.org_W7112574406]. Concurrently, the security landscape of post-quantum       
cryptography is being reassessed, with improved dual lattice attacks demonstrating that the security levels of       
leading LWE-based schemes like Kyber, Saber, and Dilithium may fall below NIST thresholds[^10.5281_zenodo.6493704].  
Advanced encryption systems are also being designed to integrate post-quantum cryptographic strategies alongside     
classical algorithms to mitigate threats from Grover's and Shor's algorithms[^10.56975_tijer.v13i3.161368].          
-                                                                                                                    
-## Quantum Internet and Networking                                                                                  
-                                                                                                                    
-The conceptualization of a global quantum internet is advancing, promising ultra-secure connectivity and the        
transmission of information encoded in quantum states across distributed quantum                                     
computers[^10.31695_ijerat.2025.9.1]. Tracking the emergence of these technologies, analyses of open software        
repositories and financial news provide pivotal insights into the evolving trends and industrial adoption of quantum 
computing[^10.1007_978-3-031-90727-2_20].                                                                            
-                                                                                                                    
-## Historical Perspectives and Applications                                                                         
-                                                                                                                    
-Foundational reviews continue to elucidate the core principles of quantum computing, explaining superposition,      
entanglement, and the transition from classical digital logic to qubit-based computation[^10.5120_ijca2021921834].   
